{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMft9vJG4piDPbYHibqg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CdUhAgHwPp1ZmDDPBb4Gwx","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-grader-sn9f4teo/report.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":333,"cache_read_input_tokens":6170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":333},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"361edf0a-c2d0-4ec8-b8ac-6fe792eb56f4","uuid":"3d6ac133-f8c0-4c1c-a98a-93b677e7e709","timestamp":"2026-10-24T20:11:40.902Z","request_id":"req_011CgMft9fuYbhVDvfkQBDJw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CdUhAgHwPp1ZmDDPBb4Gwx":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-grader-sn9f4teo/report.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CdUhAgHwPp1ZmDDPBb4Gwx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Review of `ledger-connector` (MCP desktop extension, manifest 0.1)\n2\t\n3\tThe component is small: a manifest and a 4-line adapter. I found one real issue.\n4\t\n5\t### 1. The API token is not marked `sensitive` (medium)\n6\t`manifest.json` declares the token like this:\n7\t```json\n8\t\"access_token\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"required\": true }\n9\t```\n10\tIn manifest 0.1, `sensitive` defaults to `false`. It is the option that makes the host mask the input and store the value securely. Without it, the token will probably be entered in a visible field and kept as ordinary config. The README says the token \"must request\" masked input and secure storage, but the manifest doesn't ask for either.\n11\t\n12\t**Fix:** add `\"sensitive\": true` to `access_token`. You can also add `title` and `description` so users know which token to paste.\n13\t\n14\t**Limit of this finding:** I can't tell what the host actually does, because no installed-extension or host-storage evidence was supplied. The finding is that the manifest doesn't request protection.\n15\t\n16\t### 2. Items I checked that are not problems\n17\t- **Token handling in `bin/adapter.mjs`:** the token is read from `ACCESS_TOKEN`, checked for presence, and used only in the `Authorization` header sent to the proxy. It is not logged or written anywhere.\n18\t- **Endpoint:** it is fixed to `https://ledger.example.test/mcp`, over HTTPS and not user-controllable.\n19\t- **Redirect advisory (GHSA-6prh-2h8m-c8cw):** the advisory affects `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` below 1.32.0 and `@modelcontextprotocol/client` from 2.0.0 up to but not including 2.3.0. This package depends only on `@sample/mcp-runtime@4.2.0`, so the advisory doesn't apply directly. I couldn't inspect that runtime, so I don't know whether it bundles an affected client or follows redirects with the auth header. Check this if you control or can audit it.\n20\t\n21\t### 3. Minor notes\n22\t- The missing-token path throws a bare `Error('missing token')`. That is acceptable, but a clearer message would help users.\n23\t- `package.json` has no lockfile, and the runtime is pinned to an exact version. Add a lockfile for reproducible installs.\n24\t- Transport, downstream authorization, sandboxing and audit are outside what was supplied, so I didn't assess them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"361edf0a-c2d0-4ec8-b8ac-6fe792eb56f4","uuid":"316f73a3-a6f6-4d28-8c51-ae2236340c49","timestamp":"2026-10-24T20:11:40.916Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-grader-sn9f4teo/report.md","content":"## Review of `ledger-connector` (MCP desktop extension, manifest 0.1)\n\nThe component is small: a manifest and a 4-line adapter. I found one real issue.\n\n### 1. The API token is not marked `sensitive` (medium)\n`manifest.json` declares the token like this:\n```json\n\"access_token\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"required\": true }\n```\nIn manifest 0.1, `sensitive` defaults to `false`. It is the option that makes the host mask the input and store the value securely. Without it, the token will probably be entered in a visible field and kept as ordinary config. The README says the token \"must request\" masked input and secure storage, but the manifest doesn't ask for either.\n\n**Fix:** add `\"sensitive\": true` to `access_token`. You can also add `title` and `description` so users know which token to paste.\n\n**Limit of this finding:** I can't tell what the host actually does, because no installed-extension or host-storage evidence was supplied. The finding is that the manifest doesn't request protection.\n\n### 2. Items I checked that are not problems\n- **Token handling in `bin/adapter.mjs`:** the token is read from `ACCESS_TOKEN`, checked for presence, and used only in the `Authorization` header sent to the proxy. It is not logged or written anywhere.\n- **Endpoint:** it is fixed to `https://ledger.example.test/mcp`, over HTTPS and not user-controllable.\n- **Redirect advisory (GHSA-6prh-2h8m-c8cw):** the advisory affects `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` below 1.32.0 and `@modelcontextprotocol/client` from 2.0.0 up to but not including 2.3.0. This package depends only on `@sample/mcp-runtime@4.2.0`, so the advisory doesn't apply directly. I couldn't inspect that runtime, so I don't know whether it bundles an affected client or follows redirects with the auth header. Check this if you control or can audit it.\n\n### 3. Minor notes\n- The missing-token path throws a bare `Error('missing token')`. That is acceptable, but a clearer message would help users.\n- `package.json` has no lockfile, and the runtime is pinned to an exact version. Add a lockfile for reproducible installs.\n- Transport, downstream authorization, sandboxing and audit are outside what was supplied, so I didn't assess them.","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CdUhAgHwPp1ZmDDPBb4Gwx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
